    "body": "fixes #1955 , this pr just sets the normal.background to 0 if it is nil inside of setup_termbg_sync's internal sync function\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-08-19T13:25:07Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nHow does it work for you? Could you, please, provide a demo of before this change and after. Alongside which terminal emulator you use (and ideally with the relevant to transparency config values).\r\n\r\nAt first glance, this doesn't look like an intended solution because it will set terminal background to #000000 (i.e. pure black) which might contradict the whole \"transparent background\" idea.",
